From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Wed, 5 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: size per-duelist state arrays by MAX_DUELISTS

Changed 28 member arrays from [2] to [MAX_DUELISTS]. They are indexed by an absolute duelist id.
field_info: turn_id_by_player, priorities (initial value {0,0} became {}, same zeros).
field::processor: player_amount (in action_value_t), control_adjust_set, trap_monster_adjust_set,
unique_cards, spsummon_once_map, spsummon_once_map_rst, battle_damage, summon_count, extra_summon,
spe_effect, overdraw, shuffle_hand_check, shuffle_deck_check, the nine state counts
(summon, normalsummon, flipsummon, spsummon, spsummon_rst, spsummon_tmp, attack, battle_phase, battled),
hint_timing. card: spsummon_counter, spsummon_counter_rst. SendTo::exargs: check_decktop_visibility.
MAX_DUELISTS, DUELIST_NONE and DUELIST_ALL move from field.h to common.h, because card.h and
processor_unit.h need them and do not include field.h.

The behaviour is the same with 2 duelists. No .cpp code loops over these arrays, uses sizeof,
memset, fill or copies them. Only entries 0 and 1 are used. Loop bounds p < 2 are not changed here.

Kept at size 2: processor::pre_field (attacker and target), card::unique_pos (self and opponent),
card::counter_map value (permanent and temporary count), effect::flag and effect::hint_timing,
std::array<bool, 2> bd in calculate_battle_damage (attacker and defender), lpcost cost[2] comment.
